Aelius: [Positive] Hestia, I'm here!
Hestia: Oh, Aelius. You made it in.
Hestia: I was worried you were going to have some doubts about being here after your last shift.
Aelius: What? Why would I not want to show up? This place is growing on me!
Hestia: I don’t know, I suppose I just overthought everything and was worried you’d… hate me.
Aelius: [Negative] Hestia... no...
Aelius: [Negative] How could I hate you?
Hestia: If I tried to do something like that with the others, I’d be getting the silent treatment for a century or two.
Hestia: I also ended up thinking a lot about what you said about apologizing.
Aelius: Hestia, it's ok. I'm alright.
Hestia: I knew it was the reason for a lot of my issues, but I just wanted for my family to feel like a family.
Hestia: I guess in my mind, letting them have their way would help bring us all as a family together…
Aelius: [Positive] Well, if it makes any difference, I consider you family.
Hestia: I just wish that- what?
Aelius: [Positive] I consider you family.
Hestia: I appreciate you saying that, but we don’t have the same family ties such as your mother or father. The Olympians have a diff-
Aelius: [Positive] We don’t have to have those kinds of ties to be family.
Aelius: [Positive] Family is what you want it to be, Hestia. That’s what being here in Olympus is starting to teach me.
Aelius: [Positive] You’re like another mother to me, and you care so much about everyone around you. You need to see the good about yourself, too.
Hestia:  I suppose that makes sense… but I still don’t fully understand this family concept you’re talking about. I’ll need some time to process it…
Aelius: [Positive] To put it short, family is the people you care about, not just your immediate relatives. That’s all there is to it.
Hestia: Hmmmmm... oh!
Hestia: Speaking of family, do you remember me mentioning asking Iris for a favor the other day?

-> I remember. (deference)
    Hestia: Excellent! All this talk just reminded me of what it was about!
-> Err- It may have slipped my mind. (humorous)
    Hestia: Oh, that’s alright, but our conversation just now reminded me of what it was about!
-> Not at all. (aggressive)
    Hestia: Well, that’s okay. Our conversation just now reminded me of what it was about.

Hestia: I had asked Iris to connect me to Hades so I could ask him for a favor!
Aelius: Hades? I haven’t met – or even really heard about – him before now.
Hestia: He’s in the Underworld and doesn’t really get to come up here too often, but as I’m sure you know, he is the god of the Underworld and the dead.
Aelius: What does he have to do with anything?
Hestia: I thought I’d ask him for a favor – a favor for you, really.
Hestia: I asked him if you could see your mother soon, and he agreed.
Aelius: [Positive] I can see my mom again!?
Hestia: Yes, dear. You will get to see your mother again soon.
Hestia: Hades and his wife, Persephone, weren’t too keen on the idea at  first, but after I had told them everything you’ve done so far to help everyone up here, they agreed to allow an exception.
Hestia: Hades is a <i>reeeaaaalllll</i> sticker for the rules.
Aelius: [Positive] Thank you so much, Hestia, you don’t know how much this means to me!
Hestia: Well, Hades didn’t give me a specific time, so don’t get too excited yet.
//DING sound

Hestia: As much as I’d love to have you back here all day, I think someone just came in. Judging by their footsteps, I think it’s Hermes, but don’t quote me on that.
Hestia: I’m sure you know the drill already, so I’ll let you head up front now!
Aelius: [Positive] Will do, I’ll see you in a bit! Thanks again, Hestia!
